Elsewhere - Dependencies and Libraries

Repository: JMLee1231/codeboxhack Project directory: elsewhere

Project Overview

Elsewhere is an Expo / React Native application targeting iOS, Android,
and web. It uses TypeScript and React. Native maps use
react-native-maps, while the web version uses Leaflet.

Runtime Dependencies

@expo-google-fonts/dm-sans (^0.4.2) - Provides the DM Sans Google font
for Expo/React Native.

@expo-google-fonts/dm-serif-display (^0.4.2) - Provides the DM Serif
Display Google font for Expo/React Native.

@expo/metro-runtime (~57.0.15) - Expo integration/runtime support for
the Metro JavaScript bundler.

@expo/vector-icons (^15.0.2) - Icon library bundled for Expo
applications.

@react-native-async-storage/async-storage (2.2.0) - Persistent local
key-value storage. - Used by the app for information that remains on the
user’s device.

@types/leaflet (^1.9.22) - TypeScript type definitions for Leaflet. -
Listed as a runtime dependency in this project’s package.json even
though type packages are normally development-time dependencies.

expo (~57.0.20) - Core Expo framework and tooling used to run and build
the React Native app.

expo-clipboard (~57.0.1) - Expo API for reading/writing clipboard
content. - Supports features such as copying guide text and links.

expo-font (~57.0.3) - Expo font loading and management support.

expo-linking (~57.0.9) - Handles URLs and links between the application
and external resources.

expo-location (~57.0.16) - Provides device geolocation/location
permission APIs. - Used for the app’s “My location” map functionality.

expo-status-bar (~57.0.1) - Controls the native device status bar from
the Expo application.

leaflet (^1.9.4) - Interactive JavaScript mapping library. - Used for
the web version of the application’s map. - The project uses
OpenStreetMap map tiles.

react (19.2.3) - Core React UI library.

react-dom (19.2.3) - React renderer for browser/DOM environments. -
Required for the web version of the application.

react-native (0.86.3) - Cross-platform native application framework used
for iOS and Android.

react-native-maps (1.27.2) - Native map component for React Native. -
The README states that native builds use react-native-maps and Apple
Maps on iOS.

react-native-safe-area-context (~5.7.0) - Provides safe-area
measurements/insets so UI avoids notches, status bars, home indicators,
and other device screen boundaries.

react-native-web (^0.21.2) - Implements React Native components and APIs
for web browsers.

Development Dependencies

@types/node (^26.4.1) - TypeScript type definitions for Node.js APIs.

@types/react (~19.2.2) - TypeScript type definitions for React.

tsx (^4.23.13) - Executes TypeScript/TSX directly in Node.js. - Used by
this project to run tests: tsx –test src/core/*.test.ts

typescript (~6.0.3) - TypeScript compiler and type checker. - Used by
the project’s typecheck script: tsc –noEmit

